<title>USA: Mercury Air to record Q4 charge.</title>
<headline>Mercury Air to record Q4 charge.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mercury Air Group Inc said Wednesday it will record a special fourth quarter charge of between $0.05 and $0.07 per share on a fully diluted basis, related to the bankruptcy filing of Sun Jet International Inc.</p>
<p>It said the charge will include losses from both an unsecured accounts receivable from the sale of jet fuel, and an equity investment in the company.</p>
<p>Mercury also said that the loss of Sun Jet's business will have no material impact on Mercury's future revenues or earnings going forward.</p>
</text>
